      <abstract>The Welsh Congregational Church in the Fairview hamlet of Centerville, Allegany
        County, New York, was gathered in 1846. In 1847, the first church building was constructed
        on the southern corner of Findlay Road and County Line Road. New church buildings were
        constructed closer to the Fairview hamlet in 1865 and again in 1902. The church dissolved
        around 1930. This collection contains administrative and membership records and includes
        financial records, meeting minutes, and membership records.</abstract>
